{
  "_comment": [
    "The one grammar of a threshold value, `value[:severity]` (#3071, #3457): split at",
    "the LAST `:`, trim both halves (exactly the characters of `trim_code_points`),",
    "lower-case an ASCII suffix; no `:` is warning; a suffix outside `severities` is an",
    "unreadable value (`ok` false). `value_part` / `severity` are splitThresholdSeverity's",
    "halves. `grammar_ok` is whether `value_part` is in the grammar of a threshold number,",
    "the recipe contract's patterns.thresholdNumber (pkg/config/recipe_contract.json):",
    "decimal only — an optional sign, ASCII digits with at most one `.` (at least one digit,",
    "at most 20 in all, every digit counted, leading and trailing zeros too), an optional",
    "`e`/`E` exponent of any number of digits. `float_ok` is whether parseThresholdNumber",
    "reads it: in the grammar AND finite (#3140: `1e999` is in the grammar and is +Inf).",
    "`custom_alert_disabled` is whether resolveOneCustomAlert reads the threshold as the",
    "opt-out (errCustomAlertDisabled); `row_disabled` is whether a threshold row with the",
    "value switches its key off (thresholdRowDisabled, #3141: `disable:\u003cseverity\u003e` does not);",
    "`severities` is config.ThresholdSeverities(); `trim_code_points` is every character",
    "Go's strings.TrimSpace trims (JavaScript's trim() and Python's strip() trim other sets).",
    "⛔ Never hand-edit those columns: add a row with only `value`, then run",
    "`DA_REGEN_THRESHOLD_VALUE_MATRIX=1 go test ./pkg/config -run TestThresholdValueMatrix`",
    "in components/threshold-exporter/app, which writes them from Go.",
    "Four readers are held to it. Go: pkg/config/threshold_value_parity_test.go (the file",
    "says what Go says; the row resolvers, custom alerts and the subtree overlay agree) and",
    "cmd/da-guard threshold_values_test.go (`da-guard threshold-values`). JavaScript:",
    "tools/portal/tests/threshold-value-matrix.test.ts (the RecipeBuilder's reader).",
    "Python and the JSON schema: tests/shared/test_threshold_value_parity.py",
    "(_lib_validation.threshold_number, the reading the unit-sanity lint gets from",
    "`da-guard threshold-values`, backtest --tenant's reading of served-values, the",
    "severity sets, and tenant-config.schema.json thresholdScalar's pattern)."
  ],
